In article <2uekhgINN3af@srvr1.engin.umich.edu>, mneylon@azure.engin.umich.edu (Michael K. Neylon) writes:

>It could be done.  If a good random generator is programmed in, such that
>the same series of numbers is generated given the same seed, then stuff
>such as...
>
>	dungeon creation
>	item generation
>	monster generation
>
>would all use this rnd # gen, while monster actions, chance of hitting, 
>damage, etc, would all use the system rand().  This would be a start
>at insuring that all levels, monsters, and generated items are the same.
>
No, wouldn't work. Monsters are generated randomly while you are cruising
aroud the level. So if your two players simply spend different time on 
level 1 and one of them gets an extra random monster generated, you are
screwed.
If you exclude random monster generation - you'll still get screwed if the
players visit levels in differet order (say one falls 3 levels through a
trap door, or even goes to mines immediately, while other continues with
the main dungeon).
Item generation may give you some headaches w.r.t Artifacts - if the game 
decides to generate an artifact (rare, I know) it has to check first if it
already exists in the game, so you have another potential branching point
in your random numbers.
Finally remember that monster generation depends not only on the dungeon
level, but also on player's level. So even if you ensure that the players 
enter the same level with the same random seed - they'll still may get
a different set of monsters if they are of different levels.

Actually I think the last point culd be THE idea: When starting a game in
'tournament' mode nethack generates all locations of special levels and
a random number for every level and writes that to a file. Now when a player
enters a tournament the file is read, an each time the player enters a new
level, the random number generator is re-seeded with the number found in the
for this level. A dungeon shape is generated first, this ensures that
you get at least this identical. Items should be identical as well (I hope
they get generated before monsters - but am not sure) up to the artifact 
problem, and monsters - well, they will be identical up to player level,
but after some time spent on the level they'll cease to be identical...
This is much easier and uses up less space then initial generation of the 
whole dungeon .
